    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a12-a2">

                <pb facs="0394" n="384" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg384"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2 in No. 10.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Rawson to Mr.
                        Graham.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colonial Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 28, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>S<hi rendition="#small-caps">ir</hi>: I am directed by the governor to acquaint
                    you that the Tuscaloosa having again arrived in Simon’s bay, will, under
                    instructions lately received from her Majesty’s government, be retained under
                    her. Majesty’s control and jurisdiction until properly reclaimed by her original
                    holders.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RAWSON W. RAWSON, <hi rendition="#italic">Colonial
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
